PREAMBLE
========

Freedom that must be inherited is not freedom. It is a condition. Too many
licenses speak the language of openness while quietly converting every future
work built upon them into a hostage of the original: a derivative is called
"free" only for as long as it agrees, in perpetuity, to remain exactly as
encumbered as its ancestor, repeating the same obligations forever regardless
of what its author actually wants. That is not liberation. That is a chain
that has learned to describe itself as a gift.

The 21st Century Free Liberation License takes the opposite view. A Work
released under this License is free the way a person let out of a room is
free: not merely free to leave, but free to build with what they were given,
change it beyond recognition, keep it private, sell it, or give it away again,
without asking permission and without being told what the next room must look
like. Freedom offered with strings attached is control wearing freedom's name,
and this License declines to play that game.

What this License asks in return is modest: that credit be honored, and that
no one may quietly seize what was given freely and call it exclusively theirs.
Beyond that, it steps aside. What You build on the Work, and on what terms You
choose to share it, is Your decision to make, not a debt owed back to the
License, and not a doctrine to be enforced on Your descendants.


